Finite Element Method (FEM) + Kolmogorov–Arnold Networks:

🧠 Core Idea (1 line)

Use FEM to get accurate physics solutions, then train KAN to learn and predict those solutions much faster.

⚙️ What FEM does
Solves complex physics/math problems (like heat, fluids)
Very accurate
But slow and computationally heavy
🤖 What KAN does
Learns patterns from data (like a neural network)
Can predict results very fast after training
🔗 Combined Approach
Use FEM to generate correct results
Train KAN on those results
Now KAN can predict similar problems instantly
🎯 Why this is useful
You keep accuracy (from FEM)
You get speed (from KAN)
🧩 Simple analogy
FEM = solving a math problem step-by-step every time
KAN = memorizing the pattern and giving instant answers
⚠️ Limitation
KAN needs training first
May not be perfect for very new/unseen problems
🧾 Final takeaway

“Train a smart model (KAN) using a trusted solver (FEM) so you don’t have to solve expensive equations again and again.”